 "notes": "Black hole superradiance constraint on ultralight boson mass and self-interaction, derived from BH spin posteriors. Canonical AxionMass plane: x=ULB mass mu [eV], y=inverse decay constant f^-1 [GeV^-1]; paper f matches canonical f_a (Eq.12: m_a=5.69 ueV at f=1e12 GeV, same as m_a=5.7 ueV*(1e12/f_a)). Curve is the closed boundary of the 95% credible EXCLUDED region for M33 X-7, EQUILIBRIUM scenario (the paper-preferred self-interaction model; bosenova is disfavoured), traced as a vector contour from Fig.4 right panel (exclusions.pdf, solid black contour, drawing 466 main loop). Region: mu ~1.7e-13 to 3.0e-12 eV, f^-1 up to ~1.5e-13 GeV^-1; floor at f^-1~1e-19 is the plot boundary (free-field/no self-interaction limit, i.e. standard mass exclusion). Validated: paper text gives marginalized 1D interval 0.6 peV < mu < 3 peV; upper end 3 peV=3.0e-12 matches, 2D region extends to lower mu as the paper states. The paper ALSO presents a second, weaker excluded region from IRAS 09149-6206 (first use of this SMBH) at mu ~1.7e-19 to 6e-19 eV (Fig.4 left panel, drawing 217); M33 X-7 chosen as the primary/strongest result (featured in Figs.4,5,6). BHSR is independent of DM density. A small disconnected excluded dot near f^-1~1e-11 GeV^-1 was omitted.",
